  "scope_id": "PARITY-CORRECTION-20261031-001",
  "title": "Parity's weighted family is hard, also where parity fails",
  "subject": "Whether parity's coupling family on cubic systems is easy, and whether parity's recognisable failures make any of it easy",
  "conclusion": "Counting parity's coupling (weight lam per line missing its parity) on connected simple cubic systems is polynomial exactly at lam in {0, 1, -1, i, -i, oo} and #P-hard at every other complex lam, since the theta substitution turns it into the knot's coupling at lam + 1/lam - 1. It stays #P-hard on systems where parity fails, because a parity certificate survives grafting into any host, so parity's recognisable failures select nothing.",
